Add a problem to an existing challenge
Request bodies are capped at 4 MB. If a challenge has many problems or large test cases, create it with the first problem (or a small batch) and add the remaining problems one request at a time. Each call creates a new problem, appends it to the end of the challenge and returns the saved problem with its _id. The problem object takes the same shape as an entry in problems above.

curl --location 'https://api.onecompiler.com/v1/challenges/<challenge_id>/problems?access_token=<your_access_token>' \
--header 'Content-Type: application/json' \
--data '{
    "problem": {
        "title": "Sum of two numbers",
        "markdown": "Read two integers from STDIN and print their sum",
        "properties": {
            "problemType": "code",
            "score": 5,
            "difficultyLevel": "easy",
            "options": {
                "code": {
                    "validations": [
                        { "id": 1, "input": "2 3", "output": "5", "label": "easy" }
                    ],
                    "problemCategory": "programmingLanguages"
                }
            }
        }
    }
}'
